      origins: 'Zanga is a four-player card game and a relative of Hombre and Tresillo. It is played in Spain in the region north of Malaga (Cuenca del Río Campanillas), in villages such as Villanueva de la Concepción, Almogía and Campanillas, and is also popular in the Canary Islands. The Malaga version uses a 32-card Spanish pack; the Canary Islands version uses the full 40-card pack with Tresillo-style ranking.',
